  "mathematical_review": [
    "All K_n inherit their ambient compact Hausdorff topology in the final union; inclusions are embeddings.",
    "Compact Hausdorff shrinking is proved by finite separation of a point from the complement and finite covering of C; closures are compact because they are closed in a compact stage.",
    "Two finite-cover operations give an open factor rectangle containing a compact product and lying inside its open neighbourhood.",
    "Compact A_n,B_n remain compact in successor stages by compatible subspace inclusions; recursive extensions keep A_n×B_n inside the given W.",
    "Earlier interiors are absorbed in later ones, so the displayed U∩K_m formula is correct even for m<n0; every union term is relatively open in K_m.",
    "For U×V membership the maximum stage index puts both factors into one A_n×B_n; continuous stage inclusions prove the reverse topology inclusion.",
    "Product-final equality now makes multiplication continuous; inversion was already stagewise continuous. Group closure follows the rank bounds.",
    "Escaping points can be chosen distinctly outside K_n because a finite earlier list is contained in a later stage; every subset of them is final-closed, contradicting compact Hausdorff closed-subspace compactness.",
    "Coordinate orbit continuity follows a uniformly bounded Hilbert tail plus finitely many coordinate continuities. Trace coefficients are actual finite sums of diagonal coefficients, and at most k nonidentity eigenvalues give 2k/d.",
    "Rank-one reflections are explicitly determined by each nonzero ξ_d and produce displacement2 on K1; no new choices are hidden in these operators.",
    "The LCH proof is unchanged; normalized-coefficient supplier supplies the strict compact-uniform ε²/2 estimate. Consumer forward argument uses continuous coefficient compact attainment, ensuring a strict sup bound from pointwise strict inequalities."
  ],
